 "claim": "Placements in one switching class (computed exactly). HANDLE-COUNT A's generator, run under hash seeds 0 to 23, gives each of TRISUM-READ's 17 glues one glue whose Pfaffian and minimal signings all lie in one switching class, and gives 11 of the glues two or three placements of their atoms that are not isomorphic as spaces, 25 in all. On the five glues whose alternative placement is mapped here (38 to 56 points), the native creation maps of the two placements agree exactly on the block of glue lines, so creation between glue lines sees only the switching class; but the whole maps are never isomorphic, neither with the glue's lines fixed nor under any bijection. The difference lies in atom removals: removing a line of an atom creates differently at glue lines, so native creation reads where the atoms sit, while removing a glue line creates at the atom lines with the same multiset of vectors in both placements. TRISUM-READ's frozen statements P1 to P7 hold on all five alternative placements. The other placements, 56 to 60 points, are left to a follow-up.",
